[["Map",1,2,45,46],"blog",["Map",3,4,15,16,25,26,35,36],"bank2curb",{"id":3,"data":5,"body":11,"filePath":12,"digest":13,"deferredRender":14},{"title":6,"description":7,"buildDate":8,"pubDate":9,"updatedDate":10},"Bank 2 Curb","Journal entry",["Date","2025-08-23T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"\u003Cdiv id=\"main_body\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n    \n        \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">\n            August Bank Holiday Weekend\n        \u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I set myself the challenge of concreting two obstacles over the Saturday and most of Sunday with backfill preparations made throughout the week. Although I succeeded, ultimately I overstretched myself and Sunday’s concrete suffered.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n            \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The design for the bank2curb must have come from Dan Mirza’s repeatedly requesting a “slope/incline” to decked curb combined with inspiration from Paul Carroll bank to curb obstacle at his new spot.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The curb stones already existed at Brickside and just needed transporting. I can’t say for sure how much each one weighs but I managed to get 3 in my the back of the Seat Ibiza without crushing any part of myself and doing limited damage to the car which made me feel like a world’s strongest man contestant.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/curbs_car.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            At one point when unloading at the other end, I almost tripped backwards with a curb stone leaning against me which would have been a very bad outcome if it had fallen on me.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I had done a mock up of the backfill cross section at brickside to calculate how many red bricks I would need. That came to about 160.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/tetris.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/tetris2.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/tetris3.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            There was a pile of cleaned bricks at Brickside and one load in my car is about 60 bricks, so that means putting 15-20 in a wheelbarrow/on a skateboard, rolling them to the car, stacking them in the boot, driving 5mins up the river, unloading them onto the skateboard and rolling them up the lane to their next resting place.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/bricks_curbs.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/bricks_curbs2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Ch2>23rd August\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            First job was to establish the foundation. This meant laying a row of 26 red bricks side by side on a bed of ballast and cement mix to try to prevent any movement over time. Then went on the curb stones lined up at the edge of the row of bricks, leaving 10mm between the curbs to fill with a poly resin? later.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/foundations.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/foundations2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Behind the first row of bricks was placed another lengthways row of bricks that would support the next level of backfill bricks. This layer was laid side by side on their sides, requiring about 39 bricks to bring the level up high enough. For the deck/back section, the total red bricks needed to accommodate the 3 curb stones came to 78.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            By noon I had the shuttering in place to contain the deck and make for easy screeding and levelling. In the recess I placed a variety of rocks and loose render that had fallen from the walls at the spot, and then on top of that I laid a section of heras fence as rebar.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/deck_backfill.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/deck_backfill2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I imagine I went home for lunch at that point and after my return for the afternoon shift, I had the concrete deck in and level by 3pm.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/deck_conned_top.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I pressed on into the afternoon, laying out the remaining red bricks for the bank backfill, then adding the stones and rubble for in between the gaps, got the heras fence rebar ready and chipped out the tarmac to create a lip for the bank transition.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/bank_backfill.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The sound of me chiselling into the floor attracted the attention of workers from the reclaimed brick yard on the other side of the wall and they came to see what I was up to and essentially gave me their blessing to carry on.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Carry on I did and by 8pm the bank was in and had been seen to by the finishing trowel. It been a 12 hour day with 0 assistance other than some passing moral support.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/all_con_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/all_con_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The build had been successful but I knew I had much more to come the following day and I was quite unprepared.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/next_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/next_centre.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/next_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/dry_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/dry_left_low.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>                \n\n    \u003C/div>\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/bank2curb.mdx","f26bc3b6dc30fbf1",true,"bank2curb_wings",{"id":15,"data":17,"body":22,"filePath":23,"digest":24,"deferredRender":14},{"title":18,"description":7,"buildDate":19,"pubDate":20,"updatedDate":21},"Bank 2 Curb Wings",["Date","2025-08-28T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"\u003Cdiv id=\"main_body\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/leftwing_backfill.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/rightwing_backfill2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_ima÷ge\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/leftwing_backfill2.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/rightwing_backfill.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal÷_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/leftwing_backfill3.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Although the curbs, deck and bank were set and curing nicely through the late summer days, the obstacle was not finished. To be able to take advantage of 100% of the grindable curb space, wings would be required and I hardly delayed in getting them in.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/leftwing_backfill4.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/backfill_soil_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/backfill_soil_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Wednesday 27th, I had the shuttering figured out and the backfill and heras rebar prepared. Thursday 28th after work, I was ready to go and managed to get a hand from Yangchen, who exchanged his help for an interview for his dissertation.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/wang_shov.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/yang_shov2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            We were concreting at 7.30 and since the right wing went in quickly and Yangchen was down for more we pressed on and got the left wing done on the same night, finishing around 10.30. \n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/yang_wing.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/yang_wing2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/yang_wing3.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I hadn’t made up my mind whether to make the wings into a roll on grind but Yangchen wanted it so I went with it and was pleased with the result so I asked him to write the Chinese characters of his name on the roll on grind as a momento. \n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/yang2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/yang3.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>    \n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/next_wings.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/next_wings_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>  \n\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/next_wings2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/cured.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/cured2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/cured_front.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n        \n        \u003Ch2>Reflections\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_main/dried.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n\n    \u003C/div>\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/bank2curb_wings.mdx","967dc6eb40a1d5ff","day1",{"id":25,"data":27,"body":32,"filePath":33,"digest":34,"deferredRender":14},{"title":28,"description":7,"buildDate":29,"pubDate":30,"updatedDate":31},"First Build",["Date","2025-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightbox from \"../../components/ImageLightbox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"main_body\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n        \n        \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">{`\n            August 16th\n        `}\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The desperate burst of effort at Otherside was doomed to be a deadend. I had planned to start building there on Saturday but on Thursday night I had noticed signs of the inevitable. With no intention to put money into a lost cause, I moped for the morning wondering what to do and eventually decided to scope out a pedestrianised road 1/2 a mile up river that I'd heard Pat mention in the past.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n\n        \u003CImageLightbox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/firstday_road.jpeg\" />\n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/firstday_road.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I went down for a reccy, saw the existing retaining wall and the soft tarmac and the road barrier already down there asking to be backfill and decided to send it. I hauled 75 red bricks from Brickside in my car and set up the formers.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_noforms.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_bricks.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            There were plentiful rocks and hardcore for the small back fill. I had a wire net and some leftover heras fence for rebar. \n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_close.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            By 6.30pm I had the materials for concrete, water and a shovel and began mixing up on the tarmac.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_rebar.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            By 8.30pm the shaping was done. 2x ballast2:sharp1:0.5cement mixes and 1x sharp1:10mmgravel1:0.5cement mixes. The ballast mix for the body and the gravel for the coping and the transition. The tarmac already had a lip so there was no need to chip out a recess for the transition concrete.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_right_medium2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_face.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_right_medium.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_left_high.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The coping was shaped with a tool made from a cyclindrical water bottle screwed to a bit of batten for a handle. I'd first used this improvised coping tool on the big QP at Brickside. Although it served me well, its fundamental flaw was its flimsiness and the fact I was afraid it might break mid-build.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/coping_left_dark.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The concrete had gone in well and no one who passed by had been offended by me building.\u003Cbr>\u003C/br>The spot was a goer.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cimg class=\"landscape_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_far_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n    \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n        \n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_right2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_front_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/coping_next_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/coping_next_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_front.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n        \n        \u003C/div>\n    \n    \u003C/div>\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/day1.mdx","4d8f944a189fef9d","expansion2",{"id":35,"data":37,"body":42,"filePath":43,"digest":44,"deferredRender":14},{"title":38,"description":7,"buildDate":39,"pubDate":40,"updatedDate":41},"Conny QP Extension",["Date","2025-08-24T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"\u003Cdiv id=\"main_body\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            On Monday evening I reclaimed two more road barriers and the following evening hauled 110 red bricks from the Otherside piles.    \n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/backfill_bricks3.jpeg\">\u003C/img> */}\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_bricks4.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_bricks2.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_bricks5.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">August 24th\u003C/h2>\n            \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            To my demise, that afternoon I was driving to Halifax for a gig and was not even backfill ready at 10.      \n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_rocks.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            With great solo effort, by 3pm the concrete was sufficiently shaped and finished. The coping is wonky because of my flimsy not fit for purpose coping shaping tool. And the deck is proud on the right side because I ran out of time. But it would go.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_right_low.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_coping_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_left_full.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_coping_left.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_coping_left_close.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/con/con_front.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    \n            I made the bold choice to leave the qp uncovered mid afternoon of bank holiday Monday and within 2 hours someone who'd gone to inspect the spot themselves sent me a photo of a strange racist message written by finger in the concrete. When I returned from the gig that night I stopped by to check for more damage and had to patch some tags scratched into the both sides of the face. It would take a few more attacks before I never left any fresh concrete uncovered.\n        \n        `}\u003C/p>\n        \n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/next/next_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/next/next_face.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/next/next_left_wide.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/next/next_coping_right.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n            \u003Cimg class=\"journal_image\" src=\"./src/assets/images/conxtension/next/next_left_full.jpeg\">\u003C/img>\n        \u003C/div>\n        \n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    \n            The coping is wobbly as anything but and the right side of the face is a bit lumpy but a week before there wasn't a whippy quarter pipe in Sheffield and now there was.\n        \n        `}\u003C/p>\n            \n    \u003C/div>\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/expansion2.mdx","2ed1c3d02b72b91c","meta::meta",["Map",47,48,49,50,51,52],"astro-config-digest","{\"root\":{},\"srcDir\":{},\"publicDir\":{},\"outDir\":{},\"cacheDir\":{},\"site\":\"https://example.com\",\"compressHTML\":true,\"base\":\"/\",\"trailingSlash\":\"ignore\",\"output\":\"static\",\"scopedStyleStrategy\":\"attribute\",\"build\":{\"format\":\"directory\",\"client\":{},\"server\":{},\"assets\":\"_astro\",\"serverEntry\":\"entry.mjs\",\"redirects\":true,\"inlineStylesheets\":\"auto\",\"concurrency\":1},\"server\":{\"open\":false,\"host\":false,\"port\":4321,\"allowedHosts\":[]},\"redirects\":{},\"image\":{\"endpoint\":{\"route\":\"/_image\"},\"service\":{\"entrypoint\":\"astro/assets/services/sharp\",\"config\":{}},\"dangerouslyProcessSVG\":false,\"domains\":[],\"remotePatterns\":[],\"responsiveStyles\":false},\"devToolbar\":{\"enabled\":true},\"markdown\":